1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,920
You and two colleagues each have something impressive to show.

2
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,660
But one built for self-service, another planned a staffed

3
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:11,540
launch, and a third changed the connection the others depend on.

4
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:14,360
AI helped everyone move faster.

5
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:18,020
Now the team has a week of untangling to do.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,820
Nobody meant to create that work.

7
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:23,900
Each person can now lead a much larger

8
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,400
contribution, with agents helping build it.

9
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:29,980
But the decisions reach across other people's plans.

10
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,600
A faster team needs a better way to agree what

11
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,220
matters, and what each person can depend on.

12
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,680
We're learning to work more like leaders of connected teams.

13
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:41,380
What deserves investment?

14
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:42,720
Who owns the outcome?

15
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,140
What can we rely on from each other?

16
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:48,580
Greater production capacity hasn't given us more

17
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:51,260
attention, or instant experience making those calls.

18
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:54,220
We need each other's judgment more than ever.

19
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:58,200
The Converge methodology is a shared way of working,

20
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:01,240
using the agents and tools you already have.

21
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:03,200
Agree on a worthwhile outcome.

22
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:06,740
Give people complete contributions to own, with room to act.

23
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:10,400
Make the promises between those contributions clear.

24
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:13,220
Bring expertise into important decisions,

25
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:15,560
prepared well enough that a colleague can help.

26
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:18,680
A vision describes the outcome and experience we want.

27
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:21,480
Contracts capture the promises we depend on.

28
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:24,380
A working mock can make them easier to judge.

29
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:29,140
The same agreements align colleagues and guide their agents, so what

30
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:32,100
we decide together can shape the work after the conversation ends.

31
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:37,180
Agents help expose missing direction, investigate choices, and carry

32
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:40,860
authorized work through implementation, coordination, checking, and repair.

33
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:44,180
Their capabilities need to fit the responsibility.

34
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,740
The team still needs evidence that its contributions work together.

35
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,860
Several impressive demos don't establish a usable service.

36
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:55,780
We should see the benefit in practice: useful outcomes,

37
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,500
fewer repeated explanations, less rescue work.

38
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:02,360
If a review queue keeps growing, reconsider the commitments.

39
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:06,440
If the destination changes, work from where we are toward what matters now.

40
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:09,740
The way we collaborate should improve as we learn.

41
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Try it on a project you already share.

42
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:16,100
Open the Converge methodology with your agent.

43
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:21,100
Ask it to prepare one short agreement: the next useful outcome,

44
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:24,120
who owns each part, and what they need from each other.

45
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:28,280
Resolve the important differences together, then get moving.